malcolmr.google@cse.unsw.edu.au (Malcolm Ryan) writes:
> Yet another old idea I'd like to toss around again. We all know you
> can poison arrows and daggers by dipping them in a potion of sickness.
> What about other potions? In particular, it would make sense to make
> potions of sleep, paralysis and confusion useful in this fashion.
> 
> The patch would be simple enough. It would mean expanding the
> obj->opoisoned flag to more than one bit, which would break save
> compatibility unless there is another unused field we could store the
> value in. There is a comment in obj.h that indicates that there are 6
> free bits after "bypass". Perhaps it could be fit in  there without
> breaking anything. (Can this be guaranteed, or is it likely to be
> system dependent?)

I'd be inclined to reuse (with a #define) the recharged bitfield
(which currently only has meaning for wands, tools, and corpses); that
gives you eight distinct effects to play with, assuming that you can
only coat a missile with one type of potion at a time.

